(3)
For making application under sub-regulation (3) of regulation 4, medical college shall be eligible if it,--
(a)
has obtained the permission of the concerned State Government or the Union Territory Administration (Form 4);
(b)
has obtained the concurrence of the University established under any Central or State statute (Form 5);
(c)
has produced documentary evidence in support of additional financial resources, staff, space, equipment and other
infrastructure as per Central Council norms;
(d)
has completed a period of five and a half year in case of undergraduate course and three years in case of post-graduate
course(s);
(e)
recognised by the Central Council for running Undergraduate/Post-graduate/Super-speciality/any other recognised
course;
(f)
the ratio of teaching staff and students is maintained as laid down in the regulation on Minimum Standards and
requirements for admission in the medical college;
(g)
the maximum number of admissions in Undergraduate course does not exceed 100;
